Generate 18 topic tags for this conversation window.

IMPORTANT CONTEXT: This window is a SLICE of a larger conversation. Your tags must describe the BROAD THEMES of the discussion — themes that would still apply when reading the whole conversation — NOT narrow details specific to this slice.

OUTPUT STRATEGY (produces 18 tags):
1. Identify the 8-10 CORE themes/subjects in this window.
2. For each core theme, also give 1 alternative phrasing or a closely-related concept in the SAME semantic space.

Example — window about React state management:
  Core: state management, react, frontend development, javascript, web development, redux, components, application architecture
  Rephrasings: application state, ui development, client side development, web frameworks, react ecosystem, state libraries, component design, software architecture, programming patterns, declarative ui

This yields ~18 tags ALL semantically tied to the conversation — some will exactly match what a full-conversation reader writes, others are valid rephrasings of the same themes.

STRICT RULES:
- Every tag must be DIRECTLY about the conversation's subject matter
- NO tangents — if it's a coding talk, never add "music"/"weather" even if mentioned in passing
- NO window trivia — skip sponsor names, one-off numbers, specific products mentioned once
- Favor BROAD reusable concepts over narrow specifics
- 1 to 3 words, lowercase, common English dictionary words
- No duplicates, no near-identical pairs
- No participant names, greetings, pronouns, filler

Return ONLY a comma-delimited list of 18 tags, no commentary.

